# Security Baseline

When touching auth, uploads, user content, secrets, or AI tools:

- Authn ≠ authz — check ownership/roles on every sensitive operation
- Parameterize queries; sanitize HTML; validate redirects/URLs
- CSRF protections where cookie sessions apply
- No secrets in client code, git, or logs
- SSRF: do not fetch arbitrary user URLs server-side without allowlists
- File uploads: type/size/path constraints
- AI: treat model/tool output as untrusted; prevent prompt injection from user content escalating privileges

Full checklist: `docs/workflows/security-review.md`
